		"id": "unreviewed-journal-disclosure",
		"title": "Journal data reaches user-facing reads without review",
		"cause": "Data written to a shared journal or event log can be read or forwarded to a user-facing surface by any actor because the read and notification paths have no review or approval gate.",
		"criteria": "A site exhibits this cause when journaled flags, blockers, or similar entries become visible in user-facing reads or notifications without an intervening review decision. This qualifies whether the missing gate is in the write path, the read path, or the notification path.",
